# Git Workflow — Chave Project

## Branch Rules

**NEVER commit or push directly to `main`.** All work happens on a dedicated branch.

### Branch Naming

```
feat/T001        # new feature — branch from main
fix/T001         # bug fix — branch from main
release/v1.0.0   # release — branch from main
```

Always branch from `main`:
```bash
git checkout main && git pull origin main
git checkout -b feat/T001
```

The user is responsible for opening Pull Requests. When a ticket is done, inform the user so they can open the PR.

## Commit Standard

Every commit **must** reference the ticket number and type:

```
feat-T001: setup project React + TypeScript + Vite
fix-T002: resolved env config not loading in mock mode
hotfix-T016: resolved crash on home screen QA
```

Format: `<type>-<ticket>: <short description in English>`

| Prefix | When to use |
|---|---|
| `feat-TXXX` | New feature or implementation |
| `fix-TXXX` | Bug fix |
| `hotfix-TXXX` | Critical crash or production fix |

### Rules

- Description must be clear and in English
- Use present tense ("resolved", "setup", "add", "remove")
- One logical change per commit — do not bundle unrelated changes
- Do not commit generated files, build artifacts, or `node_modules`
- Do not commit `.env` files containing real values (only `.env.example`)

## Changelog

After each completed ticket, update `Changelog.md` at the project root:

```markdown
## [v1.0.0] — In progress

- feat-T001: setup project React + TypeScript + Vite
- fix-T002: resolved env config not loading in mock mode
```

## Checklist Before Every Commit

- [ ] Working on a feature/fix branch (not `main`)
- [ ] Commit message follows `<type>-<ticket>: <description>` format
- [ ] No unrelated files staged
- [ ] `Changelog.md` updated with this ticket's entry
- [ ] Tests pass (`npm test`)
